# This repo root is shared with a large amount of unrelated content (other
# clients' scripts, a separate landing/dashboard web project, WordPress theme
# assets, stray html/md/json/tsx files, etc) alongside the actual Centrio
# Electron app. Prettier's default file coverage (html/css/md/json/yml/...)
# is much broader than ESLint's, so instead of trying to enumerate every
# unrelated path, ignore everything by default and re-include only the
# Centrio app's own JS sources. This also keeps explicitly protected files
# (index.html, styles.css, locales/**) untouched by `prettier --write`.
*

!/*.js
!/eslint.config.js
!/.prettierrc.json
bundle.js
bundle.js.map

!/main/
!/main/**

!/renderer/
!/renderer/**

!/scripts/
!/scripts/**
